ization without understanding.\"\r\n    ],\r\n    \"difficulty\": 2\r\n  },\r\n  {\r\n    \"id\": \"Q218\",\r\n    \"subarea\": \"Literature & Understanding\",\r\n    \"objective\": \"Language Acquisition, Transfer, and Cross-Curricular Language Development\",\r\n    \"stem\": \"Which instructional practice best develops metacognitive reading skills?\",\r\n    \"options\": [\"Silent reading logs\", \"Think-aloud modeling\", \"Dictation practice\", \"Listening tests\"],\r\n    \"correctIndex\": 1,\r\n    \"rationales\": [\r\n      \"Silent reading logs track reading but don't model metacognition.\",\r\n      \"Correct! Think-aloud modeling explicitly demonstrates comprehension monitoring and strategy use.\",\r\n      \"Dictation doesn't develop metacognitive awareness.\",\r\n      \"Listening tests assess, not develop, metacognition.\"\r\n    ],\r\n    \"difficulty\": 2\r\n  },\r\n  {\r\n    \"id\": \"Q219\",\r\n    \"subarea\": \"Literature & Understanding\",\r\n    \"objective\": \"Language Acquisition, Transfer, and Cross-Curricular Language Development\",\r\n    \"stem\": \"A student writes 'She no like apples.' This shows:\",\r\n    \"options\": [\"Code-switching\", \"Negative transfer\", \"Fossilization\", \"Overgeneralization\"],\r\n    \"correctIndex\": 1,\r\n    \"rationales\": [\r\n      \"Code-switching alternates complete languages, not creates errors.\",\r\n      \"Correct! Negative transfer from Spanish (no auxiliary verb needed) causes this English error.\",\r\n      \"Fossilization is persistent errors despite instruction, not initial transfer.\",\r\n      \"Overgeneralization applies learned rules too broadly, not L1 interference.\"\r\n    ],\r\n    \"difficulty\": 2\r\n  },\r\n  {\r\n    \"id\": \"Q220\",\r\n    \"subarea\": \"Literature & Understanding\",\r\n    \"objective\": \"Language Acquisition, Transfer, and Cross-Curricular Language Development\",\r\n    \"stem\": \"Integrating reading, writing, speaking, and listening into science lessons supports:\",\r\n    \"options\": [\"Language across the curriculum\", \"Grammar immersion\", \"Phonemic awareness\", \"Spelling transfer\"],\r\n    \"correctIndex\": 0,\r\n    \"rationales\": [\r\n      \"Correct! Language across the curriculum integrates literacy skills into all subject areas.\",\r\n      \"Grammar immersion isn't a recognized approach.\",\r\n      \"Phonemic awareness is specific to sound-letter relationships.\",\r\n      \"Spelling transfer relates to word patterns, not cross-curricular integration.\"\r\n    ],\r\n    \"difficulty\": 2\r\n  },\r\n  {\r\n    \"id\": \"Q221\",\r\n    \"subarea\": \"Literature & Understanding\",\r\n    \"objective\": \"Language Acquisition, Transfer, and Cross-Curricular Language Development\",\r\n    \"stem\": \"Which describes students using both Spanish and English within a conversation?\",\r\n    \"options\": [\"Interlanguage\", \"Code-mixing\", \"Negative transfer\", \"Pidgin\"],\r\n    \"correctIndex\": 1,\r\n    \"rationales\": [\r\n      \"Interlanguage is a learner's evolving system, not mixing languages in speech.\",\r\n      \"Correct! Code-mixing blends elements from two languages within discourse.\",\r\n      \"Negative transfer causes errors, not intentional mixing.\",\r\n      \"Pidgin is a simplified contact language, not bilingual mixing.\"\r\n    ],\r\n    \"difficulty\": 2\r\n  },\r\n  {\r\n    \"id\": \"Q222\",\r\n    \"subarea\": \"Literature & Understanding\",\r\n    \"objective\": \"Language Acquisition, Transfer, and Cross-Curricular Language Development\",\r\n    \"stem\": \"The teacher gradually removing supports as students gain independence is:\",\r\n    \"options\": [\"Direct instruction\", \"Scaffolding\", \"Translation\", \"Immersion\"],\r\n    \"correctIndex\": 1,\r\n    \"rationales\": [\r\n      \"Direct instruction is explicit teaching, not gradual release.\",\r\n      \"Correct! Scaffolding provides temporary support that's gradually removed as competence grows.\",\r\n      \"Trans